          "A trainer records can look finished while the next reviewer still cannot say who decided, which source was used, or when the case closed, and that gap is exactly what this control is meant to remove. The Fitness Staffing Agency team should be able to show the same trainer records case to a client, an auditor, or a new hire without rewriting the story for each audience.",
          "The case for a written trainer records control is not bureaucracy; volume hides the few items nobody can reconstruct, and gym owners, studio operators, and fitness program leaders eventually pay for that with rework. When the trainer records source is maintained by another team, the brief should name that contact and the expected response time so escalation does not become a repeated chase."
